{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>After the death.</b> As it is said: ״כטוב כחוטא״. כטוב — these are the two sons of Aharon, who died only because they ruled a halakhah in the presence of Moshe Rabbeinu, as is stated in Yoma. כחוטא — this is Korah and his congregation. These were burned and those were burned. Rabbi Acha bar Ze'ira said: this is what Iyov said: ״אף לזאת יחרד לבי ויתר ממקומו״. The sons of Aharon were not like the staff, for the staff entered the Holy of Holies moist and emerged [sprouting], as it is said: ״ויוצא פרח״. And even Titus the wicked entered in peace and emerged in peace, while the sons of Aharon entered in peace and emerged burned. As it is said: ״בחוריו אכלה אש ובתולותיו לא הוללו״. Why were the young men of the sons of Aharon consumed by fire? Because the virgins were not adorned — for how many suitable virgins sat waiting for them, and they said: 'Our father's brother is king, our father is High Priest, our mother's brother is prince, we are deputies of the priesthood — which woman is fitting for us?' And therefore they did not marry and died without sons. And it seems to me that this is why the verse repeats ״וימותו״ — meaning, without remembrance."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:16.482901350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}